WEBVTT

1
00:00:25.791 --> 00:00:30.000


2
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.833
<b>What should Arjun be mindful of?</b>

3
00:00:32.833 --> 00:00:38.583
<b>How can someone as wise as him stay away </b>
<b>from the influence of petty ambitions?</b>

4
00:00:38.583 --> 00:00:41.625
<b>This verse explains exactly that.</b>

5
00:00:41.625 --> 00:00:44.000
<b>Here, Lord Krishna says to Arjun:</b>

6
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:50.333
<b>"Action performed with desire for its fruits </b>
<b>represents the lowest level of Karma Yoga.</b>

7
00:00:50.333 --> 00:00:52.500
<b>You must rise above this.</b>

8
00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:58.416
<b>Those who act solely for results are like misers,</b>

9
00:00:58.416 --> 00:01:00.500
<b>forever in misery.</b>

10
00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:05.041
<b>You should instead take refuge in Buddhi Yoga,</b>
<b>established in divine wisdom."</b>

11
00:01:09.791 --> 00:01:11.958
<b>Krishna is cautioning Arjun</b>

12
00:01:11.958 --> 00:01:16.250
<b>to stay away from actions that lead to sin.</b>

13
00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:20.416
<b>Through Buddhi Yoga, or the </b>
<b>path of selfless action,</b>

14
00:01:20.416 --> 00:01:24.458
<b>this can be achieved by remaining </b>
<b>vigilant to your duty.</b>

15
00:01:24.458 --> 00:01:29.958
<b>who crave results and the pleasure that follows</b>

16
00:01:29.958 --> 00:01:33.291
<b>Krishna calls them misers here.</b>

17
00:01:33.291 --> 00:01:35.291
<b>A miser</b>

18
00:01:35.291 --> 00:01:41.708
<b>meaning one who, though sitting upon a </b>
<b>treasure of wealth, refuses to use it.</b>

19
00:01:41.708 --> 00:01:46.666
<b>The irony is that while wealth's very purpose </b>
<b>is to elevate one's standard of living,</b>

20
00:01:46.666 --> 00:01:50.583
<b>a miser, in their obsession to save a few coins,</b>

21
00:01:50.583 --> 00:01:54.666
<b>automatically lowers their entire quality of life.</b>

22
00:01:54.666 --> 00:01:55.708
<b>Similarly,</b>

23
00:01:55.708 --> 00:01:59.291
<b>one who acts solely for the desire of fruits</b>

24
00:01:59.291 --> 00:02:03.375
<b>loses an eternal outcome for a small gain.</b>

25
00:02:03.375 --> 00:02:05.875
<b>Had they acted without desire for results,</b>

26
00:02:05.875 --> 00:02:09.291
<b>this very same action in the form of </b>
<b>selfless Karma Yoga</b>

27
00:02:09.291 --> 00:02:12.833
<b>could have united them with the Divine.</b>

28
00:02:12.833 --> 00:02:13.500
<b>But</b>

29
00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:16.666
<b>due to their limited thinking and petty greed,</b>

30
00:02:16.666 --> 00:02:21.333
<b>they fail to utilize this endless spiritual treasure.</b>

31
00:02:21.333 --> 00:02:23.625
<b>You must have heard that saying:</b>

32
00:02:23.625 --> 00:02:26.000
<b>'One who leaves the whole for half, </b>

33
00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:28.208
<b>gets neither half nor whole.'</b>

34
00:02:28.208 --> 00:02:35.250
<b>Meaning, one who abandons the complete for </b>
<b>the partial ultimately loses both.</b>

35
00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:36.458
<b>Likewise,</b>

36
00:02:36.458 --> 00:02:43.541
<b>one who chases small results while ignoring </b>
<b>the vast treasure of spirituality</b>

37
00:02:43.541 --> 00:02:48.083
<b>ultimately ends up losing both.</b>

38
00:02:53.125 --> 00:02:59.583
<b>Humankind has been blessed with </b>
<b>the special gift of intelligence.</b>

39
00:02:59.583 --> 00:03:03.291
<b>This intelligence protects us from danger,</b>

40
00:03:03.291 --> 00:03:06.750
<b>helps us recognize good opportunities,</b>

41
00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:10.500
<b>and aids in our growth.</b>

42
00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:11.875
<b>But</b>

43
00:03:11.875 --> 00:03:20.000
<b>what if humans fail to utilize </b>
<b>this wonderful gift fully?</b>

44
00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:24.916
<b>Or worse, begin to misuse it?</b>

45
00:03:24.916 --> 00:03:29.291
<b>When one ignores their spiritual growth</b>

46
00:03:29.291 --> 00:03:35.791
<b>and uses intelligence solely for </b>
<b>worldly pleasures and desires, </b>

47
00:03:35.791 --> 00:03:41.375
<b>it becomes a grave misuse of this gift.</b>

48
00:03:41.375 --> 00:03:45.791
<b>This special blessing of intelligence</b>
<b>becomes meaningful</b>

49
00:03:45.791 --> 00:03:50.250
<b>only when we use it to avoid harmful actions,</b>

50
00:03:50.250 --> 00:03:59.458
<b>to seek spiritual shelter, and to </b>
<b>elevate our spiritual consciousness.</b>

51
00:04:04.250 --> 00:04:09.583
<b>Everyone deeply loves their family.</b>

52
00:04:09.583 --> 00:04:20.250
<b>All strive to provide their family with every </b>
<b>possible means of comfort and happiness. </b>

53
00:04:20.250 --> 00:04:21.791
<b>But</b>

54
00:04:21.791 --> 00:04:24.958
<b>have you ever considered this?</b>

55
00:04:24.958 --> 00:04:31.000
<b>That these comfort-giving means, </b>
<b>provided after so much effort,</b>

56
00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:36.958
<b>might actually be causing them harm?</b>

57
00:04:36.958 --> 00:04:40.583
<b>You must be surprised hearing this?</b>

58
00:04:40.583 --> 00:04:46.375
<b>How could this be possible?</b>

59
00:04:46.375 --> 00:04:49.750
<b>Understand through this example</b>

60
00:04:49.750 --> 00:04:52.291
<b>You spent your life struggling,</b>

61
00:04:52.291 --> 00:04:55.541
<b>earning wealth through hard work,</b>

62
00:04:55.541 --> 00:05:01.166
<b>so that this wealth could provide </b>
<b>your children a comfortable life.</b>

63
00:05:01.166 --> 00:05:02.916
<b>But what</b>

64
00:05:02.916 --> 00:05:07.208
<b>if they become too accustomed </b>
<b>to such comfort? </b>

65
00:05:07.208 --> 00:05:15.333
<b>And due to this habit, they begin to</b>
<b>shy away from any struggle?</b>

66
00:05:15.333 --> 00:05:22.666
<b>What if pride in your wealth leads </b>
<b>them toward unethical activities?</b>

67
00:05:22.666 --> 00:05:26.916
<b>All this is possible.</b>

68
00:05:26.916 --> 00:05:29.041
<b>A family head's responsibility</b>

69
00:05:29.041 --> 00:05:33.500
<b>isn't just to make their </b>
<b>children's lives comfortable,</b>

70
00:05:33.500 --> 00:05:34.166
<b>but</b>

71
00:05:34.166 --> 00:05:37.000
<b>to make it valuable too.</b>

72
00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:41.583
<b>To keep them away from unethical desires.</b>

73
00:05:41.583 --> 00:05:46.000
<b>You are like a tree for your family,</b>

74
00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:53.875
<b>a tree whose moral values' shade helps </b>
<b>small saplings grow on their own.</b>

75
00:05:53.875 --> 00:06:03.750
<b>This tree also protects these saplings </b>
<b>from the harmful sun of worldly temptations.</b>

76
00:06:08.625 --> 00:06:10.666
<b>In their professional journey,</b>

77
00:06:10.666 --> 00:06:15.958
<b>many become so selfish about their success</b>

78
00:06:15.958 --> 00:06:23.791
<b>that they overlook numerous life-enriching </b>
<b>opportunities along the way.</b>

79
00:06:23.791 --> 00:06:28.791
<b>You spend a large part of </b>
<b>your day at your workplace.</b>

80
00:06:28.791 --> 00:06:35.666
<b>Sometimes you spend more time</b>
<b>with colleagues than family.</b>

81
00:06:35.666 --> 00:06:41.375
<b>What a golden opportunity this is to</b>
<b>build such precious relationships</b>

82
00:06:41.375 --> 00:06:45.041
<b>that might stay with you lifelong,</b>

83
00:06:45.041 --> 00:06:48.250
<b>even beyond this workplace.</b>

84
00:06:48.250 --> 00:06:52.666
<b>Different kinds of people. </b>
<b>Each with their own experiences.</b>

85
00:06:52.666 --> 00:06:58.708
<b>How helpful such friends can </b>
<b>be when you're in doubt,</b>

86
00:06:58.708 --> 00:07:01.791
<b>when you need advice,</b>

87
00:07:01.791 --> 00:07:06.125
<b>or simply need to share your sorrows.</b>

88
00:07:06.125 --> 00:07:07.250
<b>But</b>

89
00:07:07.250 --> 00:07:13.583
<b>a person blinded by selfishness sees these </b>
<b>colleagues either as rivals</b>

90
00:07:13.583 --> 00:07:18.041
<b>or merely as means to an end.</b>

91
00:07:18.041 --> 00:07:23.541
<b>Thus, they remain deprived </b>
<b>of the joy of relationships.</b>

92
00:07:23.541 --> 00:07:26.416
<b>They even forget that</b>

93
00:07:26.416 --> 00:07:32.666
<b>sometimes these very </b>
<b>relationships can aid in success.</b>

94
00:07:32.666 --> 00:07:37.625
<b>Even if they make false attempts</b>
<b>to build relationships,</b>

95
00:07:37.625 --> 00:07:43.875
<b>people soon distance themselves, </b>
<b>sensing their selfishness.</b>

96
00:07:43.875 --> 00:07:47.291
<b>Such people... are misers...</b>

97
00:07:47.291 --> 00:07:56.291
<b>who ignore the vast treasure of human </b>
<b>relationships for their petty self-interests.</b>

98
00:07:56.291 --> 00:07:58.625
<b>"Selfless Karma Yoga."</b>

99
00:07:58.625 --> 00:08:04.708
<b>How beautiful would it be if humans </b>
<b>simply performed their duties,</b>

100
00:08:04.708 --> 00:08:07.791
<b>without being tainted by selfishness. </b>

101
00:08:07.791 --> 00:08:15.750
<b>Then they wouldn't see their</b>
<b>colleagues as rivals or mere tools.</b>

102
00:08:15.750 --> 00:08:19.041
<b>They would respect them properly.</b>

103
00:08:19.041 --> 00:08:24.125
<b>Help them openly when needed.</b>

104
00:08:24.125 --> 00:08:27.916
<b>And this is the essence of sweet relationships</b>

105
00:08:27.916 --> 00:08:32.958
<b>you receive far more than what you give.</b>

106
00:08:32.958 --> 00:08:36.125
<b>The only condition is that</b>

107
00:08:36.125 --> 00:08:40.708
<b>the foundation of this relationship </b>
<b>shouldn't be selfishness.</b>

